# Moxa ioLogik E1240.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Moxa ioLogik E1240 Remote Ethernet I/O — 8-channel AI
# | 
# | Source: ioLogik E1200 Series User Manual V16.2, August 2025 (Appendix A)
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP (port 502); Modbus/TCP ID default = 1
# | 
# | AI channels (ch0-7), measured values in FC04 input registers:
# | FC04 addr 0-7: AI_rawValue (word, R)
# | FC04 addr 8-23 (2 words/ch): AI_scaledValue hi/lo (u32, R)
# | FC04 addr 24-31: AI_rawValueMin (word, R)
# | FC04 addr 32-39: AI_rawValueMax (word, R)
# | FC04 addr 60-67: AI_status (word, R; 0=normal,1=burnout,2=over range,3=under range)
# | FC04 addr 109-124 (2 words/ch): AI_scaledValueMin hi/lo (u32, R)
# | FC04 addr 125-140 (2 words/ch): AI_scaledValueMax hi/lo (u32, R)
# | FC01 addr 4145-4152: AI_resetMinValue ch0-7 (1=reset min; R/W)
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Moxa
@model=ioLogik E1240
@description=8-AI remote Ethernet I/O, Modbus/TCP. FC04: AI_rawValue ch0-7 (addr 0-7), AI_scaledValue u32 hi/lo (8-23), AI_rawValueMin (24-31), AI_rawValueMax (32-39), AI_status (60-67; 0=normal,1=burnout,2=over range,3=under range), AI_scaledValueMin (109-124), AI_scaledValueMax (125-140). FC01: AI_resetMinValue (4145-4152), AI_resetMaxValue (4153-4160). FC03: AI_mode ch0-7 (addr 24-31; 0=0-10V,1=4-20mA,2=0-20mA,4=4-20mA burnout), AI_burnoutValue u32 hi/lo ch0-7 (addr 40-55).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/moxa-iologik-e1240.toml; Source: ioLogik E1200 Series User Manual V16.2, August 2025 (Appendix A). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
